        <mxCell id="v34" value="&lt;b&gt;Notes&lt;/b&gt;&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; Module 9 changes a lifecycle state only through ILifecycleCommands.apply_decision() (one writer of lifecycle events, A8). A reversal or an overturned appeal never rewinds the loan: ReversalService flags the outcomes that came from the reversed decision through IOutcomeFlags, and the next assessment no longer counts them (ES-11).&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; Possession is offered only when the stored previous state allows it (ADR-0009, proposed): ACCEPTED &amp;#8594; NOT_HANDED_OVER; ACTIVE or RETURN_INITIATED &amp;#8594; WITH_BORROWER, RETURNED or LOST.&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; Timer values (response window, appeal window) are configuration, proposed in FR/NFR v1.4.&lt;br&gt;&amp;#8226; The evidence trail is derived from the event log, never stored separately (UC-D6). Search and ranking are Student 1's and Student 2's; Student 3 only logs and evaluates them." style="shape=note;size=12;whiteSpace=wrap;html=1;fontSize=10.5;align=left;verticalAlign=top;spacingLeft=8;spacingTop=4;fillColor=#F4F6F8;strokeColor=#8C99A6;" vertex="1" parent="1">
          <mxGeometry x="390" y="1175" width="650" height="190" as="geometry" />
        </mxCell>
